  "correct": "B",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Mark where a sine wave reflects onto itself",
      "body": "<p>A vertical line through a maximum or a minimum reflects the sine curve onto itself. These are points where the entire sine input equals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>, for an integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Both peaks and troughs supply vertical symmetry axes.",
      "pitfall": "A zero crossing is not a vertical line of symmetry.",
      "pause": "Set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l06",
          "reminder": "Vertical symmetry axes of sine occur at phase <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Work with the entire angle input",
      "body": "<p>Rearrange the phase condition for the horizontal coordinate, retaining its integer parameter. Remember that the input multiplier affects both the shift and the spacing.</p>",
      "recap": "Translate the whole trigonometric input back to the original variable.",
      "pitfall": "The constant subtracted inside the sine is not by itself the horizontal shift.",
      "pause": "Derive the family of symmetry-axis coordinates and use it to search near the origin.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l15",
