    {
      "title": "Search neighbouring phase indices",
      "body": "The integer in a phase family may be negative even when the resulting horizontal coordinate is positive.",
      "recap": "To find the first positive member, locate the last nonpositive member and the next one.",
      "pitfall": "Starting with integer zero can skip valid axes nearer the origin.",
      "pause": "Find the neighbouring integer indices yourself and prove your selected axis is the least positive one.",
